    "name": "Question Stem Training",
    "text": "2\nQuestion Stem Training\n3+ SECTIONS\nInstructions\n\nIdentify all the LR question stem types and their associated Back Up Plans in a section*.\n\nFor instance, after reading a Weaken question stem, say, \"Weaken. Does this make the conclusion less likely to be true?\"\n\nDo not look at the stimulus or answer choices.\n\nThis is not the time to attempt to answer the question.\n\nGo to the LSAT Question Database to check your question stem identifications.\n\nOn the stems you get wrong, write down(on your scratch paper or using this template):\n\nThe exact text of the stem you misidentified\n\nYour wrong question stem identification\n\nThe correct question stem identification\n\nHow you could know the correct identification next time\n\nReview the stems you misidentified and how you could identify them correctly before every Question Stem Training workout.\n\nOnly stop Question Stem Training once you can reliably hit 100% question type and Back Up Plan identification accuracy on three sections in a row.\n\nSEE FULL WORKOUT DETAILS",
