    "name": "Acronym LR Section",
    "text": "3\nAcronym LR Section\nInstructions\n\nNOTE: The Acronym is a way to hold yourself accountable to following the LR Full Question Process (outlined below).\n\nWrite the Acronym on a piece of scratch paper to keep next to you during LR sections*.\n\nFor each question, check off each letter as you do that step in the process.\n\nThe Acronym\n\nR - Read\n\nT - Translate\n\nQ - Quip\n\nC - CLIR\n\nQ - Question Type\n\nP - Powerful-Provable \n\nM - Mission\n\nJust say what the correct answer would be according to this stimulus specifically\n\nFor Strengthen/Weaken, set a goal for the answer to hit\n\nA - Answer Choice Translation and quipping\n\nB - Back Up Plan\n\nHow to Apply the Back Up Plan: Talk through why and how the Back Up Plan standard applies to this answer using specific nouns and verbs from the stimulus\nSEE FULL WORKOUT DETAILS",
