    "name": "Unofficial Diagramming Marathon",
    "text": "4\nUnofficial Diagramming Marathon\nInstructions\n\nLook back at your most recently used LR sections to identify the questions that allow an opportunity for diagramming.\n\nReattempt these questions with a new mindset, one that embraces diagramming as a useful tool.\n\nTry diagramming a few borderline stimuli, even if you aren't sure they should be diagrammed.\n\nThis is how you learn the line between where diagramming is helpful and where it's not helpful.\n\nThe Unofficial Diagramming Marathon only ends when you no longer feel any hesitation to diagram, there is no fear of diagramming left, and diagramming seems boring and rote.\n\nSEE FULL WORKOUT DETAILS",
